# Prettier now runs over the whole repo (`prettier --check .`), so what it must
# NOT touch has to be stated here rather than encoded in a narrow glob that
# quietly leaves most of the repo unformatted.

node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated or run-local: handbook work dirs and demo output.
work/
runs/
examples/work/

# pnpm owns this file's formatting.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The internal engineering journal, specs and review notes. Hand-written prose
# where a leading `+` means "plus" mid-sentence — which CommonMark reads as a
# list marker, so normalising it inserts a blank line and splits the sentence in
# half. A formatter cannot tell that apart from a list, and there is nothing to
# gain by reflowing a document nobody publishes. Left alone deliberately.
docs/internal/

# The analyzer's fixture repo. These files are deliberately written in the idiom
# of the language being parsed — reformatting them would change what the
# analyzer tests are asserting about real-world source.
examples/demo-project/

# Three hand-authored, self-contained HTML documents. Prettier's HTML printer
# reflows inline elements, which is a rendering change we cannot verify from a
# formatter run — and all three are verified by eye, not by a test. Reformatting
# them is a deliberate, separately reviewed change, not a side effect of `pnpm format`.
docs/handbook-deck.html
docs/index.html
packages/studio/public/index.html
